          "summary": "Add frequency, notice, cost and no-system-access limits to IBM's investigation right in § 11.3",
          "comment": "[Playbook] We added the standard guardrails on investigations of our use: no more than once in any twelve-month period, on fifteen (15) days' written notice, during business hours, by an independent investigator under confidentiality, at IBM's cost unless an underpayment above 10% is found, and with no access to our systems. Our playbook does not permit unlimited or unannounced audits or vendor access to Customer systems; we are happy to discuss a shorter notice period where IBM has a good-faith, documented suspicion of unlawful Content.",
